WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.030
Dominoes, Quick Starter, The Skateboarder, by Christine Lindop.

00:09.080 --> 00:11.070
CHAPTER I

00:11.120 --> 00:28.790
No Skateboard

00:28.840 --> 00:34.150
After Hannah's house, there's a new skate park.

00:34.200 --> 00:43.470
A lot of young people in the town go there after school with their skateboards.

00:43.520 --> 00:50.070
These days, Hannah often goes there with her cousin, Justin.

00:50.120 --> 00:54.270
Justin goes to school with her.

00:54.320 --> 01:00.390
Hannah doesn't like school very much, or getting up early.

01:00.440 --> 01:08.830
She's always late, and she doesn't have many friends.

01:08.880 --> 01:16.870
But with the new skate park, she's suddenly very interested in skateboarding.

01:16.920 --> 01:24.190
The only thing is, Hannah has no skateboard.

01:24.240 --> 01:28.150
Sometimes, Justin asks Hannah,

01:28.200 --> 01:33.030
Hey, do you want to get on my skateboard?

01:33.080 --> 01:40.430
So she does, but not for long.

01:40.480 --> 01:45.870
She doesn't want to fall off in front of everybody.

01:45.920 --> 01:52.110
So usually, she watches the skateboarders.

01:52.160 --> 01:55.110
Owen is 15.

01:55.160 --> 01:58.030
He's a good skateboarder.

01:58.080 --> 02:04.510
He can do a lot of tricks.

02:04.560 --> 02:09.990
I love Owen's skateboarding. Hannah thinks.

02:10.040 --> 02:15.830
I want to jump and do tricks, too.

02:15.880 --> 02:21.830
Why don't you have a skateboard, Hannah? Justin asks her.

02:21.880 --> 02:26.270
That's a new thing for me. Skateboarding.

02:26.320 --> 02:28.550
Hannah answers.

02:28.600 --> 02:30.590
Then she thinks.

02:30.640 --> 02:33.230
My birthday's coming.

02:33.280 --> 02:50.870
Maybe I can talk to Mom and Dad.

02:50.920 --> 02:52.670
After two.

02:52.720 --> 02:54.310
Good grades.

02:54.360 --> 03:12.510
Better presents.

03:12.560 --> 03:18.470
On Hannah's birthday morning, she opens her presents.

03:18.520 --> 03:23.910
There's a big present from her mother and father.

03:23.960 --> 03:28.470
Hannah opens it first, excitedly.

03:28.520 --> 03:31.830
Wow.

03:31.880 --> 03:33.030
She cries.

03:33.080 --> 03:35.030
A skateboard.

03:35.080 --> 03:36.190
Thanks.

03:36.240 --> 03:44.550
Well, your school grades are good, Hannah. Her mother says.

03:44.600 --> 03:47.160
And it is your birthday.

03:47.520 --> 03:51.870
So, happy birthday, honey.

03:51.920 --> 03:55.270
Now, open that present.

03:55.320 --> 03:59.910
Her father says, it's from Evan.

03:59.960 --> 04:02.830
Hannah opens it.

04:02.880 --> 04:05.350
It's a helmet.

04:05.400 --> 04:09.470
Awesome. Hannah cries.

04:09.520 --> 04:14.550
But her older brother, Evan, laughs.

04:14.600 --> 04:20.510
You like watching skateboarding videos, I know. He says.

04:20.560 --> 04:25.390
But do you skateboard?

04:25.440 --> 04:30.110
Yes, I do. Hannah says hotly.

04:30.160 --> 04:34.870
Sometimes I'm Justin's skateboard.

04:34.920 --> 04:38.830
And I have my skateboard now.

04:38.880 --> 04:42.430
So I can do more.

04:42.480 --> 04:47.830
Can you jump or do tricks? Evan asks.

04:47.880 --> 04:51.870
Can you go fast and stay on?

04:51.920 --> 04:56.670
Duh. Hannah answers her brother angrily.

04:56.720 --> 05:00.230
What dumb questions?

05:00.280 --> 05:06.270
Evan, honey, please. Their mother says.

05:06.320 --> 05:09.910
It's Hannah's birthday.

05:09.960 --> 05:15.390
OK. Evan says.

05:15.440 --> 05:23.790
That weekend, Hannah takes her new skateboard to the skate park with Justin.

05:23.840 --> 05:26.670
There aren't many people there.

05:26.720 --> 05:30.630
Hannah is excited.

05:30.680 --> 05:31.670
OK.

05:31.720 --> 05:33.270
Let's go.

05:33.320 --> 05:39.910
Justin says, the two cousins begin skateboarding.

05:39.960 --> 05:43.670
Justin does a trick.

05:43.720 --> 05:48.270
Hannah skateboards up and down.

05:48.320 --> 05:53.710
Maybe I can jump now. She thinks.

05:53.760 --> 05:56.270
She goes faster.

05:56.320 --> 05:57.880
Then she jumps.

06:00.600 --> 06:05.590
But she falls off her skateboard.

06:05.640 --> 06:11.550
When Hannah is on the ground, somebody laughs.

06:11.600 --> 06:13.270
Oh, no.

06:13.320 --> 06:15.590
They're laughing at me.

06:15.640 --> 06:20.110
This is awful. She thinks.

06:20.160 --> 06:23.270
She gets up quickly.

06:23.320 --> 06:27.270
I'm going. She tells Justin.

06:27.320 --> 06:30.430
And she leaves.

06:30.480 --> 06:35.790
Just then, Owen arrives with his friends.

06:35.840 --> 06:42.230
They're laughing at a picture of Owen on his phone.

06:42.280 --> 06:46.110
But Hannah's far away now.

06:46.160 --> 06:50.790
No more skateboarding for me. She thinks.

06:50.840 --> 07:06.350
Chapter 3.

07:06.400 --> 07:08.070
First Steps.

07:08.120 --> 07:29.030
The next day, Justin stays at home with his family.

07:29.080 --> 07:33.270
But Hannah walks past the skate park.

07:33.320 --> 07:38.230
A lot of people are doing tricks.

07:38.280 --> 07:43.950
I can't skateboard there now. Hannah thinks.

07:44.000 --> 07:48.110
She watches Owen on his skateboard.

07:48.160 --> 07:53.470
He goes up in the air and comes down again.

07:53.520 --> 07:57.230
He's awesome. Hannah thinks.

07:57.280 --> 08:00.470
And I'm awful.

08:00.520 --> 08:07.750
She leaves the skate park and begins to walk home through the park.

08:07.800 --> 08:10.750
The sun is hot.

08:10.800 --> 08:15.350
Hannah sits down on one of the park benches.

08:15.400 --> 08:18.870
The sun is in her eyes.

08:18.920 --> 08:22.310
So she closes them.

08:22.360 --> 08:29.470
When she opens her eyes again, she sees a young woman near her.

08:29.520 --> 08:34.510
She is sitting on the grass with her baby boy.

08:34.560 --> 08:38.750
The little boy is trying to stand.

08:38.800 --> 08:43.710
Good boy, Michael.

08:43.760 --> 08:48.350
His mother says, stand up now.

08:48.400 --> 08:50.350
Yes.

08:50.400 --> 08:52.950
That's right.

08:53.000 --> 08:56.830
Michael stands up slowly.

08:56.880 --> 09:02.270
He takes one little step and falls down.

09:02.320 --> 09:06.270
Oh, come on now, Michael.

09:06.320 --> 09:10.630
His mother says, don't cry.

09:10.680 --> 09:13.670
Try again.

09:13.720 --> 09:18.430
Michael stops crying and laughs.

09:18.480 --> 09:23.310
He takes his mother's hand and stands up again.

09:23.360 --> 09:26.550
Good boy, Michael.

09:26.600 --> 09:32.710
His mother says, Michael sits down suddenly.

09:32.760 --> 09:39.710
He laughs and claps his hands happily.

09:39.760 --> 09:44.070
Hannah watches them for five minutes.

09:44.120 --> 09:52.670
Michael stands up and falls down again and again.

09:52.720 --> 09:55.830
Try again, Michael.

09:55.880 --> 10:04.670
His mother says, he doesn't stop falling, but it doesn't matter.

10:04.720 --> 10:06.630
Hannah thinks.

10:06.680 --> 10:18.110
He gets up and tries again, time after time, and he's no more than a baby.

10:18.160 --> 10:22.510
Hannah leaves the park and walks home.

10:22.560 --> 10:25.710
He thinks about baby Michael.

10:25.760 --> 10:27.710
Okay.

10:27.760 --> 10:32.550
She says, I need some more skateboard practice.

10:32.600 --> 10:50.670
But where can I go for that?

10:50.720 --> 10:57.670
Chapter four, practice, practice, practice.

10:57.720 --> 11:15.630
Hmm, let's see.

11:15.680 --> 11:20.110
The skate parks no good. Hannah thinks.

11:20.160 --> 11:24.950
I want to do my practice alone.

11:25.000 --> 11:29.390
That evening, she goes for a walk.

11:29.440 --> 11:34.790
Two blocks from her house, there's an office building.

11:34.840 --> 11:40.550
At half past five, everybody in it goes home.

11:40.600 --> 11:46.350
They drive all their cars out of the parking lot.

11:46.400 --> 11:56.230
Hey, I can skateboard here. Hannah thinks.

11:56.280 --> 12:03.190
The next evening, she takes her skateboard and helmet with her.

12:03.240 --> 12:06.990
I'm going out for some skateboard practice.

12:07.040 --> 12:14.230
She tells her mother, she skateboards to the parking lot.

12:14.280 --> 12:17.270
There are no cars there.

12:17.320 --> 12:22.110
First, she skateboards slowly.

12:22.160 --> 12:28.270
She is alone and nobody is watching.

12:28.320 --> 12:33.150
This is awesome. She thinks.

12:33.200 --> 12:38.630
After an hour, she goes home.

12:38.680 --> 12:41.750
She skateboards most evenings.

12:41.800 --> 12:47.190
Soon, she can go fast.

12:47.240 --> 12:51.710
One evening, she tries jumping.

12:51.760 --> 13:00.470
She skateboards across the parking lot and jumps.

13:00.520 --> 13:06.590
Suddenly, she is on the ground.

13:06.640 --> 13:11.630
A woman is going past on a bicycle.

13:11.680 --> 13:17.070
She sees Hannah on the ground and smiles at her.

13:17.120 --> 13:19.110
Bad luck.

13:19.160 --> 13:23.750
She calls, try again.

13:23.800 --> 13:33.790
So Hannah tries once more and falls off her skateboard again.

13:33.840 --> 13:40.630
She laughs, gets up and goes home.

13:40.680 --> 13:46.190
Two days later, Hannah is back in the parking lot.

13:46.240 --> 13:53.630
She jumps again.

13:53.680 --> 13:59.510
This time, she doesn't fall off.

13:59.560 --> 14:03.950
At home that evening, her mother says,

14:04.000 --> 14:08.150
You're happy about something, honey?

14:08.200 --> 14:11.710
Tell me, what is it?

14:11.760 --> 14:15.190
Well, Hannah begins.

14:15.240 --> 14:17.710
Don't laugh, okay?

14:17.760 --> 14:19.350
Okay.

14:19.400 --> 14:26.470
The practice is helping. I can do good skateboard jumps now.

14:26.520 --> 14:28.470
Usually.

14:28.520 --> 14:33.310
That's wonderful, honey.

14:33.360 --> 14:36.720
Just then, Evan comes in.

14:36.800 --> 14:38.750
Oh, no.

14:38.800 --> 14:40.670
Hannah thinks.

14:40.720 --> 14:55.950
What does he want?

14:56.000 --> 15:02.950
Chapter five, up early.

15:03.000 --> 15:19.470
Hey, how's your new skateboard?

15:19.520 --> 15:23.910
Evan asks Hannah nicely.

15:23.960 --> 15:27.150
Her mother smiles at this.

15:27.200 --> 15:30.510
Then she quickly leaves the room.

15:30.560 --> 15:34.390
Oh, it's not bad.

15:34.440 --> 15:36.550
Hannah answers.

15:36.600 --> 15:39.590
And the helmet's awesome, too.

15:39.640 --> 15:44.670
But I have a lot of bruises now, look.

15:44.720 --> 15:49.750
Evan looks at the bruises all over her arms and legs.

15:49.800 --> 15:52.790
Ouch. He says.

15:52.840 --> 15:57.030
So, do you skateboard at the skate park now?

15:57.080 --> 16:00.510
No. Hannah answers.

16:00.560 --> 16:04.590
There are always a lot of people there.

16:04.640 --> 16:07.750
But I want to go up the walls.

16:07.800 --> 16:11.710
I want to turn in the air, too.

16:11.760 --> 16:18.350
Well, I go past the skate park every day when I go to work.

16:18.400 --> 16:21.790
There's nobody there in the early morning.

16:21.840 --> 16:27.590
Evan says, Evan, that's an awesome idea.

16:27.640 --> 16:29.430
Hannah cries.

16:29.480 --> 16:35.830
I can go there before school, thanks.

16:35.880 --> 16:40.750
Next day, Hannah gets up at six o'clock.

16:40.800 --> 16:46.110
She skateboards for an hour before school.

16:46.160 --> 16:48.550
This is wonderful.

16:48.600 --> 16:52.230
Her mother says a week later.

16:52.280 --> 16:56.670
Hannah's up early every morning these days.

16:56.720 --> 17:01.550
She's never late for school now.

17:01.600 --> 17:05.710
Sometimes Hannah is tired in the morning.

17:05.760 --> 17:10.790
But then she remembers baby Michael.

17:10.840 --> 17:14.080
Babies get up early. She thinks.

17:14.160 --> 17:20.550
So, I can get up early, too.

17:20.600 --> 17:26.910
One Saturday afternoon, her cousin Justin calls her on the phone.

17:26.960 --> 17:28.990
Hey, Hannah.

17:29.040 --> 17:31.470
Are you coming tomorrow?

17:31.520 --> 17:33.150
Coming where?

17:33.200 --> 17:35.270
What's tomorrow?

17:35.320 --> 17:37.510
It's June 21st.

17:37.560 --> 17:40.790
Go skateboarding day.

17:40.840 --> 17:46.070
People all around the world are skateboarding.

17:46.120 --> 17:50.550
I'm going to the skate park with all my friends.

17:50.600 --> 17:52.350
Come with us.

17:52.400 --> 17:55.310
Okay. Hannah says.

17:55.360 --> 17:57.150
See you there.

17:57.200 --> 18:02.070
Don't forget your skateboard. Justin says.

18:02.120 --> 18:04.830
Justin, don't be dumb.

18:04.880 --> 18:20.080
That answers.

18:21.080 --> 18:44.590
It's June 21st.

18:44.640 --> 18:48.630
Hannah finds her skateboard and helmet.

18:48.680 --> 18:52.110
Then she goes to the skate park.

18:52.160 --> 18:55.110
She's excited.

18:55.160 --> 18:58.270
Can I do this? She thinks.

18:58.320 --> 19:04.590
I don't know, but I can try.

19:04.640 --> 19:10.550
At the skate park, Hannah sees Justin with some friends.

19:10.600 --> 19:13.070
She goes over to them.

19:13.120 --> 19:16.990
Hey, Hannah. Justin says.

19:17.040 --> 19:17.990
Watch this.

19:18.040 --> 19:23.110
Owen's doing a very tough trick.

19:23.160 --> 19:27.190
Owen goes up the wall and turns.

19:27.240 --> 19:30.510
He goes very high.

19:30.560 --> 19:34.030
Everybody stops and watches.

19:34.080 --> 19:37.590
Wow. Hannah says.

19:37.640 --> 19:40.630
He's awesome.

19:40.680 --> 19:44.550
Owen does a different trick now.

19:44.600 --> 19:47.070
It's an easy trick.

19:47.120 --> 19:54.230
But this time, he falls off his skateboard.

19:54.280 --> 19:58.910
He walks past Hannah and smiles at her.

19:58.960 --> 20:03.310
Everybody falls off sometimes. Owen says.

20:03.360 --> 20:06.830
Sure. Hannah answers.

20:06.880 --> 20:09.390
How do you do that trick?

20:09.440 --> 20:11.750
I want to learn it.

20:11.800 --> 20:15.790
Put your right foot here. Owen tells her.

20:15.840 --> 20:19.030
And push with your left foot.

20:19.080 --> 20:22.670
Owen helps Hannah with the trick.

20:22.720 --> 20:26.070
OK. Hannah says.

20:26.120 --> 20:30.790
I need some more practice with that, but thanks.

20:30.840 --> 20:34.590
You're a real skateboarder now, Hannah.

20:34.640 --> 20:37.720
Justin tells her quietly after that.

20:38.720 --> 20:44.470
Later, Hannah and Justin walk home through the park.

20:44.520 --> 20:48.270
Hannah sees baby Michael again.

20:48.320 --> 20:53.030
He is walking across the grass to his mother.

20:53.080 --> 20:57.670
This time, he doesn't take her hand.

20:57.720 --> 21:01.670
And he doesn't fall down.

21:01.720 --> 21:03.720
Hello.

21:04.720 --> 21:07.670
Hello. Says Hannah.

21:07.720 --> 21:10.670
She smiles at him.

21:10.720 --> 21:15.670
Can you do it again? Says Michael's mother.

21:15.720 --> 21:20.670
The baby laughs and claps his hands.

21:20.720 --> 21:26.670
I can. He says.

21:26.720 --> 21:30.720
And he stands up.

21:31.720 --> 21:35.670
Justin and Hannah walk away.

21:35.720 --> 21:39.670
Who's that? Justin asks.

21:39.720 --> 21:40.670
Now?

21:40.720 --> 21:46.670
Oh, a little baby. Hannah answers.

21:46.720 --> 21:51.720
But maybe one day, a really good skateboarder.

22:00.720 --> 22:14.720
Chapter six, a real skateboarder.

22:31.720 --> 22:35.670
It's June 21st.

